Ultimate Front-End PoC Challenge: Task & Habit Tracker + Analytics
Goal

Build a fully interactive task and habit tracker with analytics, custom rules, and smart UX-all in vanilla JS, HTML, and CSS.
Advanced Requirements

1. Task & Habit Management
Tasks:
Title, description, due date, priority
Status: active / in-progress / stalled / completed
Habits:
Name, frequency (daily, weekly, custom)
Habit streak tracker (visual progress bar or calendar)
Optional: custom rules (e.g., only track habits on weekdays)


2. Smart Sorting & Filtering
Users can filter/sort tasks and habits by:
Status
Priority
Due date
Streaks (habits)
Bonus: Multi-level filters (e.g., high-priority habits due today)


3. Interactive Dashboard
Display real-time statistics:
Number of tasks completed today
Tasks overdue
Longest habit streak
Weekly progress chart (bar or line chart, purely using CSS/JS)
Dashboard updates live as users add/remove/update tasks and habits.


4. Drag & Drop + Nesting
Users can reorder tasks and habits via drag-and-drop.
Tasks can have subtasks that can be reordered independently.
Bonus: Collapsible subtask sections.


5. Animations & Visual Feedback
Smooth animations for:
Adding/removing tasks or habits
Completing tasks (e.g., fade out, strike-through)
Dragging tasks (highlight drop target)
Hover effects and tooltips for UI elements.


6. Custom Rule Engine (Logic Layer)
Users can define simple rules:
Example: “If task priority = High and due date ≤ today → highlight in red”
Example: “If habit streak ≥ 7 → show badge”
This ensures they implement a dynamic evaluation system in JS.


7. Persistence & Undo
Save all tasks, habits, and dashboard data in localStorage.
Bonus: Implement an undo/redo stack for the last 5 actions.


8. Theme & Responsiveness
Light/Dark mode toggle.
Fully responsive layout for mobile and desktop.
Bonus: Adaptive dashboard (collapse sections on small screens).

